["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Sometimes the best move is no move. A hunter who sits the right spot, still and patient, lets the animal walk into the shot.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A map: bedding cover top left, a feeding area bottom right, and a dashed trail between them. Wind blows from the right. The hunter sits beside the trail on the downwind side. Be in before first light and stay later than you want.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wait between bed and feed</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"42\" width=\"372\" height=\"236\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"36\" fill=\"#b9c7a3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">bedding</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"200\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">feed</text><path d=\"M130 120 Q 200 140 220 170 T 270 210\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">trail</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"250.0,70.0 259.0,65.7 259.0,74.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">wind</text><g transform=\"translate(160 220) scale(0.7)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"110\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">you: downwind</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">In before first light. Stay later than you want</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sit between bed and feed, downwind of the trail (Tip).</li><li>Be there before the animal moves, and stay later than you want (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Ambush points, ground blinds, tree stands and the full body harness, calls and decoys and what is legal, coyote calling and the wind question, and patience.</li><li>Foundation lessons: <a href=\"#/s/funnels\">Trails and funnels</a>, <a href=\"#/s/pinch-points\">Pinch points</a>, <a href=\"#/s/pressure-push\">Hunting pressure</a>, <a href=\"#/s/white-tailed-deer\">Stand hunting</a> in the white tail quick lesson. Species calls: chapter 9 of each species Masterclass, for example <a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-09\">White tailed deer: how to hunt</a> and <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-09\">Ducks: how to hunt</a>.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-skills-04\">Chapter 4, Moving quietly</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-skills-06\">Chapter 6, Range and shooting positions</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six places where trails squeeze and make good ambush points: a saddle, a low gap in a ridge; a funnel, a narrow strip of cover; a creek crossing at an easy bank; a field corner nearest thick cover; a bench, a flat step on a slope; a trail junction where two routes meet. Pushed game heads for steep, thick ground far from roads.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Where trails squeeze (Tip)</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"182\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"78\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Saddle</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">low gap in a ridge</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"44\" width=\"182\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"78\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Funnel</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">narrow strip of cover</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"122\" width=\"182\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"156\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Creek crossing</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">easy bank</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"122\" width=\"182\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"156\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Field corner</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">nearest thick cover</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"200\" width=\"182\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"234\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"239\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bench</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">flat step on a slope</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"200\" width=\"182\" height=\"68\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"228\" cy=\"234\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"239\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Trail junction</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">two routes meet</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pushed game: steep, thick, far from roads (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Funnels, saddles, creek crossings, field corners, trail junctions (Tip).</li><li>Pushed game heads for steep, thick, far from roads (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ambush points in detail</summary><ul><li>A funnel squeezes travel: a narrow strip of timber, a saddle, a bench, a gap in a fence (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/pinch-points\">Pinch points</a>).</li><li>Field deer often enter at the same corner or gap nearest thick cover, with the wind in their favour (60%, hunter lore, <a href=\"#/s/farm-country\">Farmland</a>).</li><li>In a Pennsylvania GPS (Global Positioning System) study, 73% of hunters stayed within 0.5 km of a road; the average farthest point was 0.84 km (90%, <a href=\"#/s/pressure-push\">Hunting pressure</a>). Opening morning, sit the trail between the crowd and the nearest steep, thick timber (Tip).</li><li>Sit downwind or crosswind of the trail, 100 to 150 m off with a clear lane, for a rifle (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/pinch-points\">Pinch points</a>).</li><li>Mark seats and both winds on the <a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a> before the season (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A ground blind brushed in with local plants, dark inside, with one small shooting window. Tips: dark inside and dark clothes; brushed in with local cover; set early, about a week ahead. No fall risk and room for two.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A ground blind that hides you</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M90 230 L120 90 L280 90 L310 230 Z\" fill=\"#6f6a4a\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"140\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#1e1e1a\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">small window</text><path d=\"M80 232 l -12 -50 l 12 18 l 10 -40 l 6 44 l 12 -22 l -6 50 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M110 232 l -12 -50 l 12 18 l 10 -40 l 6 44 l 12 -22 l -6 50 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M290 232 l -12 -50 l 12 18 l 10 -40 l 6 44 l 12 -22 l -6 50 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M320 232 l -12 -50 l 12 18 l 10 -40 l 6 44 l 12 -22 l -6 50 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M200 232 l -12 -50 l 12 18 l 10 -40 l 6 44 l 12 -22 l -6 50 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dark inside</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dark clothes</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Brushed in</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">with local cover</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Set early</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a week ahead</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No fall risk. Room for two (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Dark inside, dark back wall, small windows: you vanish (Tip).</li><li>Brush it in and set it early so animals get used to it (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: blinds in detail</summary><ul><li>A ground blind or a natural blind of brush hides your outline and hand movement (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-03\">White tailed deer senses</a>).</li><li>Wear dark clothes inside; open only the windows you shoot through (Tip).</li><li>Set it a week ahead where you can (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-09\">White tailed deer: how to hunt</a>).</li><li>No fall risk, room for two, and a partner can watch the back (Tip).</li><li>Private land: the landowner's permission covers what you may set up and leave (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/landowner-permission\">Landowner permission</a>). Leaving a blind on Crown land: the app's Rule Book does not cover it. Ask a <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Conservation officer\">Conservation officer</button> (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Duck and goose blinds: <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-09\">Ducks: how to hunt</a> and <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">Geese: how to hunt</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Up and down the tree safely</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 1: the hunter stands at the base of the tree and inspects the stand, straps and harness with a magnifier icon, every trip.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1. Inspect stand, straps, harness</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"40\" width=\"30\" height=\"210\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"210\" y=\"120\" width=\"60\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><g transform=\"translate(110 250) scale(1.1)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"150\" r=\"22\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"166\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">every trip</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Inspect the stand, straps and harness.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 2: at the truck or base of the tree, put on a full body harness with chest and leg straps and a back tether.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2. Full body harness on first</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"40\" width=\"30\" height=\"210\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"210\" y=\"120\" width=\"60\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><g transform=\"translate(110 250) scale(1.1)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><path d=\"M103 214 L117 236 M117 214 L103 236\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"280\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">chest, legs,</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">back tether</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Full body harness on at the truck.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 3: a lifeline rope runs from above the stand to the ground. The hunter, still standing on the ground, clips the harness tether to the lifeline before the feet leave the ground and stays connected all the way up and down.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Clip in before feet leave ground</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"40\" width=\"30\" height=\"210\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<rect x=\"210\" y=\"120\" width=\"60\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<line x1=\"195\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"195\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><rect x=\"189\" y=\"244\" width=\"12\" height=\"6\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#23261f\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(232 250)\"><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-26\" width=\"5\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"2\" y=\"-26\" width=\"5\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-8\" y=\"-52\" width=\"16\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-7 -50 L7 -28 M7 -50 L-7 -28\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M226 206 C 214 200, 206 194, 199 192\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.6\"/>\n<rect x=\"191\" y=\"186\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#23261f\"/>\n<line x1=\"199\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"229\" y2=\"172\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"199\" cy=\"172\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"229.0\" y=\"150.0\" width=\"166.0\" height=\"49.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"312\" y=\"170.5\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lifeline: connected</text>\n<text x=\"312\" y=\"190.5\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ground to ground</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Clip in before your feet leave the ground.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 4: from the platform, clipped in, the hunter pulls up the unloaded rifle on a haul line, muzzle down.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4. Haul line for the unloaded rifle</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"40\" width=\"30\" height=\"210\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"210\" y=\"120\" width=\"60\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><g transform=\"translate(240 120) scale(0.9)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"250\" y=\"232\" width=\"40\" height=\"8\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">UNLOADED</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">muzzle down</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pull it up after</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">you are clipped in</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Haul line up the unloaded firearm.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Most falls happen climbing up or down, or getting in and out of the stand <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Connected the whole time. Feet on the ground to feet on the ground <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tree stand safety in detail</summary><ul><li>Wisconsin DNR (Department of Natural Resources): \"Always wear a full-body harness also known as a fall-arrest system.\" \"Always have three points of contact while climbing.\" \"Always use a haul line to raise and lower your unloaded firearm or bow\" (80%, read 2026-10-11).</li><li>Iowa DNR with the Tree Stand Safety Awareness group teaches the ABC's: Always inspect your equipment, Buckle on a full body harness, Connect to the tree before your feet leave the ground (70%, search preview).</li><li>About 60% of falls happen climbing up or down or moving into the stand; in one 13 state database, 79% of people who fell wore no harness and the rest were not attached to the tree (70%, Iowa DNR search preview).</li><li>University of Wisconsin trauma review, 1999 to 2013: 55% of tree stand injuries involved the spine; 4 of 117 patients reported any harness use (75%, Wisconsin Public Radio, 17 January 2018).</li><li>Suspension trauma, hanging in a harness, \"can occur in under 20 minutes and can be fatal\" (80%, Wisconsin DNR). Carry a suspension relief strap and a phone on you, not in the pack (Tip).</li><li>A firearm never goes up or down the tree loaded, and never on your back while climbing (80%, haul line rule).</li><li>No BC tree stand rule found in the app's Rule Book (85%, my reading). Ask a conservation officer before putting a stand on Crown land (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>My lean: a ground blind or a natural seat is safer and is plenty for BC rifle hunting. If you climb, wear the harness every time.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A table of calls and decoys in BC. Mouth or hand calls, grunt tubes and rattling: yes, 95 percent, my reading. Electronic or recorded calls: only for wolf, coyote, cougar, lynx, bobcat and Schedule C birds, 99 percent. Fake decoys: yes. Live bird decoys: no. Page 12 items 41 and 42. Study aid only.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Calls and decoys: what is legal</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"46\" width=\"372\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mouth or hand call, grunt, rattle</text><rect x=\"272\" y=\"54\" width=\"60\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Yes</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">95%</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"96\" width=\"372\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Electronic or recorded call</text><rect x=\"272\" y=\"104\" width=\"60\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b46a\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Only *</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">99%</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"146\" width=\"372\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fake decoy</text><rect x=\"272\" y=\"154\" width=\"60\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Yes</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">99%</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"196\" width=\"372\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Live bird decoy</text><rect x=\"272\" y=\"204\" width=\"60\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">No</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">99%</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">* wolf, coyote, cougar, lynx, bobcat, Schedule C birds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Page 12 items 41, 42. Study aid only</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mouth and hand calls, grunt tubes, rattling: allowed (95%, my reading).</li><li>Electronic or recorded calls: only wolf, coyote, cougar, lynx, bobcat and Schedule C birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the Rule Book lines</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Unlawful: \"To use recorded or electronic calls to hunt wildlife except wolf, coyote, cougar, lynx, or bobcat or any bird listed in Schedule C\" (99%, page 12, item 41).</li><li>Unlawful: \"To use live birds as decoys or recorded bird calls to hunt game birds\" (99%, item 42).</li><li>Fake decoys: allowed <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. A decoy is not bait <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Full table: <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book: legal methods, calls and decoys</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Animal</th><th>Call</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mule deer, white tail</td><td>Grunt, rattle, bleat</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-09\">Mule deer</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-09\">White tail</a></td></tr><tr><td>Elk</td><td>Cow mew, bugle</td><td><a href=\"#/s/elk\">Elk quick lesson</a></td></tr><tr><td>Moose</td><td>Cow call, raking brush</td><td><a href=\"#/s/moose\">Moose quick lesson</a></td></tr><tr><td>Ducks, geese</td><td>Mouth calls, decoys</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-09\">Ducks</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">Geese</a></td></tr><tr><td>Coyote</td><td>Distress, electronic allowed</td><td><a href=\"#/s/predators\">Predators</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Call less than you think (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: calling notes</summary><ul><li>Mule deer does respond to fawn distress calls (70%, Lingle, via <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-09\">Mule deer: how to hunt</a>). A careless distress call may pull does, not bucks (Tip).</li><li>Learn the cow elk mew first; it works all season (Tip, video caption).</li><li>More calling detail: chapter 9 of the <a href=\"#/s/mc-elk-09\">Elk</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-moose-09\">Moose</a> and <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-09\">Black bear</a> Masterclasses (new; the quick lessons above are the short version).</li><li>Calling pulls animals to you and makes them look for the source. Be set up, wind right, before the first call (Tip).</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JcxAklUHW8I\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How To Use a Grunt Call To Call Big Bucks</b><small>Short soft grunts. Less is more.<br>Knight &amp; Hale, YouTube, 1 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uLAA8dNF7Iw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to Cow Call with Diaphragm Elk Calls</b><small>Learn the cow mew first. It works all season.<br>Elk101, YouTube, 8 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KYonRRpoZdg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Moose Calling Strategies</b><small>Cow calls, bull grunts and raking brush for moose.<br>Bass Pro Shops &amp; Cabela's Canada, YouTube, 7 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels, your call. Left: wind in your face, with the calling area upwind; a coyote circles toward the downwind side; taught by Kevin Wilson, Outdoor Canada. Right: crosswind, with the caller off to one side; the coyote loops downwind of the caller and crosses in front of the hunter; taught by Geoff Nemnich and Heath Wood. Both say watch the downwind side.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Your call: coyote wind</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"42\" width=\"180\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind in your face</text><g transform=\"translate(104 236) scale(0.6)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"104.0,120.0 99.7,111.0 108.3,111.0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"118\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">wind</text><path d=\"M164 110 Q 184 200 124 214\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">calling area</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wilson, Outdoor Canada</text><rect x=\"206\" y=\"42\" width=\"180\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Crosswind</text><g transform=\"translate(296 236) scale(0.6)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"272.0,100.0 263.0,104.3 263.0,95.7\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">wind</text><rect x=\"276\" y=\"150\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><text x=\"283\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">caller</text><path d=\"M296 150 Q 374 130 362 180 Q 352 210 318 214\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nemnich, Wood</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Both: watch the downwind side (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Coyotes often circle to come in from downwind <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Wind in your face or a crosswind? Good callers disagree. Your call.</li></ul>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Wind in your face</th><th>Crosswind</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Idea</td><td>Scent never reaches the calling area</td><td>Coyote's downwind loop passes in front of you</td></tr><tr><td>Who says it</td><td>Kevin Wilson, Outdoor Canada <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td><td>Geoff Nemnich, Grand View Outdoors; Heath Wood, Bass Pro <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Risk</td><td>Call muffled; coyote circles behind you</td><td>Coyote may wind you if you sit too far downwind</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: both sides in their words</summary><aside class=\"callout lean\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Your call. Both setups are taught. Try each over a few dawns this winter and log where every coyote came from.</p></aside><h3>Wind in your face</h3><ul><li>Kevin Wilson (Outdoor Canada, 3 March 2025): \"Whenever possible, I try to call from a downwind position.\" A crosswind \"may be the next best play\" (65%, read 2026-10-11).</li><li>He adds that \"with either a crosswind or the wind directly in your face, your chances are good\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Nemnich lists the headwind pros: it muffles your walk in, and \"your scent is not blowing into the area you intend to call\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><h3>Crosswind</h3><ul><li>Geoff Nemnich (Grand View Outdoors, 20 June 2018) calls crosswind \"my preferred wind direction while on stand\": the call carries farther and \"the downwind side of the call is now off to your right or left, not behind you\" (65%, read 2026-10-11).</li><li>He lists headwind cons: the call \"doesn't travel as far\" and it is hard to cover the area directly downwind <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Heath Wood (Bass Pro, 2019, updated 2026): \"I prefer a crosswind\"; \"Always sit where the downwind side is visible for the shot\" (65%, read 2026-10-11).</li></ul><h3>What they agree on</h3><ul><li>Coyotes usually try to come in from downwind of the sound <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>See the downwind side. Outdoor Canada: at least 50 yd (46 m), ideally 200 yd (183 m) or more (60%, search preview).</li><li>Electronic caller in front of or upwind of you: 20 to 40 yd (Nemnich), within 50 yd (Wood), 40 to 50 yd (Mossberg) (60 to 65%).</li><li>Electronic calls are legal for coyotes (99%, Rule Book item 41). Check the season and your area first (<a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>The older <a href=\"#/s/predators\">Predators</a> lesson shows one setup of each kind. Neither is the rule (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bars of how long to sit, hunter tips: a coyote calling stand about 20 to 30 minutes; a glassing seat about an hour, then glass it again (Kirchner, onX); a morning stand from first light to mid morning.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">How long to sit? (Tip)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Coyote stand</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">20 to 30 min</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"74\" width=\"360\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"74\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Glassing seat</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">1 hour, then again</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"144\" width=\"360\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"144\" width=\"120.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Morning stand</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">first light to mid morning</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"214\" width=\"360\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"214\" width=\"360.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Glassing hour: Kirchner, onX (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Glassing seat: an hour, then again <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Coyote stand: 20 to 30 minutes (Tip).</li><li>Stand or blind: be in before first light, stay through mid morning (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: patience in detail</summary><ul><li>Kirchner glasses \"one hour at a time at each spot before moving\" (65%, onX).</li><li>Coyote stands: many callers play a sequence for 20 to 30 minutes, then move (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/predators\">Predators</a>).</li><li>Deer movement peaks around dawn and dusk (70%, <a href=\"#/s/glassing\">Glassing</a>). Mule deer activity peaks about 04:00 to 09:00 and 17:00 to 21:00 (85%, from the <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-10\">Mule deer cheat sheet</a> and its sources).</li><li>Be on the seat before legal light and stay until the end of legal light in the evening (Tip). Legal hours: <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book: legal methods</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Cold kills patience: a foam pad to sit on, a layer more than you think, hand warmers (75%, <a href=\"#/s/cold-injuries\">Cold injuries</a>).</li><li>Grandpa's rule (wisdom, from <a href=\"#/s/glassing\">Glassing</a>): \"Sit longer than you think. When you want to move, glass it one more time.\"</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Beginner</th><th>Old hand (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sits where it looks pretty</td><td>Sits where the trail squeezes</td></tr><tr><td>Arrives at sunrise</td><td>Is settled before first light</td></tr><tr><td>Calls every 5 minutes</td><td>Calls little, watches a lot</td></tr><tr><td>Climbs without a harness</td><td>Clipped in, ground to ground</td></tr><tr><td>Leaves at 8 a.m.</td><td>Stays through mid morning</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>All lines are hunter wisdom, labelled Tip.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A map: bedding cover top left, a feeding area bottom right, and a dashed trail between them. Wind blows from the right. The hunter sits beside the trail on the downwind side. Be in before first light and stay later than you want.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wait between bed and feed</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"42\" width=\"372\" height=\"236\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"36\" fill=\"#b9c7a3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">bedding</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"200\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">feed</text><path d=\"M130 120 Q 200 140 220 170 T 270 210\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">trail</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"250.0,70.0 259.0,65.7 259.0,74.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">wind</text><g transform=\"translate(160 220) scale(0.7)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-7\" y=\"-36\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"-15\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"110\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">you: downwind</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">In before first light. Stay later than you want</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Feet off the ground, harness on and bound.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 3 points of contact; 20 minutes to suspension trauma <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, short form of <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Stand hunting\">Stand hunting</button>): \"Let the animal do the walking.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Mouth call fine, wire call only for the dog line\": electronic only for coyote, wolf and the cats (99%, simplified).</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 60% of falls happen getting up, down, in or out <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 4 of 117 injured stand hunters wore a harness <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><strong>Your call</strong> (opinion): coyote wind in your face, or crosswind. Test both.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, short form of \"Less is more\" in the deer grunt call video): \"Call less, watch more.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Climbing a stand without being clipped in.</li><li>Sitting where the wind takes your scent down the trail.</li><li>Leaving the seat just before the animal arrives.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pick one funnel on the Hunt Map near home. Sit it two mornings with the wind right. Log what passed, when, and from where.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://dnr.wisconsin.gov/education/OutdoorSkills/TreestandSafety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wisconsin DNR, tree stand safety</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://iowadnr.gov/About-DNR/DNR-News-Releases/ArticleID/2044/Tree-stand-safety-focus-of-awareness-campaign\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Iowa DNR, tree stand safety focus of awareness campaign</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.wpr.org/environment/uw-study-falls-tree-stands-most-likely-result-spinal-injuries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wisconsin Public Radio, UW study: falls from tree stands (17 January 2018)</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorcanada.ca/coyotemistakes/2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Canada, coyote calling mistakes (Kevin Wilson, 3 March 2025)</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.grandviewoutdoors.com/predator-hunting/coyote/the-worst-four-letter-word-in-coyote-hunting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grand View Outdoors, wind in coyote hunting (Geoff Nemnich, 20 June 2018)</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://1source.basspro.com/news-tips/predator/7612/hunters-are-coyotes-not-responding-maybe-its-your-set\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bass Pro 1Source, coyote set up (Heath Wood)</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://resources.mossberg.com/journal/beat-the-wind-to-kill-more-predators\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mossberg, beat the wind (Brodie Swisher)</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 12 items 41 and 42, via the Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"#/sources\">Hunt Mentor research notes (summary of the sources listed in Sources)</a>.</li></ul>"]